# Preserve byte-exact line endings for parser testdata.
# The CP1252 sample file is byte-encoding-sensitive (0x92 curly apostrophe);
# the 250-row sample is line-count-asserted in tests. Keeping these as binary
# guarantees autocrlf does not rewrite LF -> CRLF on commit/checkout, which
# would change file size and break wc -l / 185-byte assertions.
internal/parse/testdata/* binary

# Enrichment parser fixtures (Phase 12) are copied byte-for-byte from
# apps-script/src/__fixtures__/ and feed the byte-parity proof (notably the
# wikitext SHA-1 check). An autocrlf LF->CRLF rewrite would change the wikitext
# bytes and flip the SHA-1, breaking parity on a fresh checkout. Keep binary.
internal/backendsrv/enrich/testdata/* binary

# Go source: enforce LF in repo to match `gofmt`/build expectations.
*.go text eol=lf

# Module files.
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Linux deploy artifacts: MUST be LF — they are scp'd to the Hetzner box. A CRLF
# shebang (#!/usr/bin/env bash\r) breaks with "bad interpreter"; systemd units
# and the Caddyfile also prefer LF.
deploy/*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/Caddyfile text eol=lf
deploy/*.service text eol=lf

# Linux watcher tarball payload (Phase 25 / LNX-05): the install.sh script and
# the systemd user unit are extracted + run on a Linux box. A CRLF shebang
# (#!/bin/sh\r) breaks with "bad interpreter"; systemd units prefer LF too.
# Keep these LF regardless of the dev box's autocrlf.
packaging/linux/*.sh text eol=lf
packaging/linux/*.service text eol=lf
